        "original_id": "0a30105c-bd1b-5139-a9c1-0a71b068afa7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Levon Helm, Jack Ridley, Ed Harris, Robert Knott, Viggo Mortensen, Renée Zellweger, Jeremy Irons\n- Films: The Right Stuff, Appaloosa, The Abyss, Glengarry Glen Ross, Apollo 13, Nixon, The Rock, Absolute Power, A Beautiful Mind, Enemy at the Gates, Radio, A History of Violence, Gone Baby Gone, The Way Back, Man on a Ledge, Gravity, Snowpiercer, Run All Night\n- Roles: Narrator, Air Force test pilot, aeronautical engineer, chief of the U.S. Air Force's Flight Test Engineering Laboratory\n- Organizations: U.S. Air Force\n\nFacts:\n- Jack Ridley was born on June 16, 1915.\n- Jack Ridley was an aeronautical engineer, a USAF test pilot, and chief of the U.S. Air Force's Flight Test Engineering Laboratory.\n- Jack Ridley died on March 12, 1957.\n- The Right Stuff is a 1983 American epic historical drama film.\n- Levon Helm narrates the introduction and other parts of The Right Stuff and also co-stars in the film as Air Force test pilot Jack Ridley.\n- Ed Harris is known for performances in The Right Stuff (1983), The Abyss (1989), Glengarry Glen Ross (1992), Apollo 13 (1995), Nixon (1995), The Rock (1996), Absolute Power (1997), A Beautiful Mind (2001), Enemy at the Gates (2001), Radio (2003), A History of Violence (2005), Gone Baby Gone (2007), The Way Back (2010), Man on a Ledge (2012), Gravity (2013), Snowpiercer (2013), and Run All Night (2015).\n- Appaloosa was directed by Ed Harris and co-written by Ed Harris and Robert Knott.\n- Appaloosa stars Ed Harris alongside Viggo Mortensen, Renée Zellweger, and Jeremy Irons.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
